△▼△▼△▼△

"―If you call yourself a father, keep your damn hands off kids!!"

The words struck harder than the fist that smashed straight into his face. Old Man Rom, witnessing this scene, imagined the pain Heinckel must have felt.

Having relied on his own endurance to take the first strike, Heinckel attempted to counter Flam and Grassis, only to be perfectly intercepted at the last moment by Gaston—or more accurately, by the girl who had "compressed" Gaston into position.

"Damn... impressive..."

While checking on the safety of the twin sisters who'd escaped Heinckel's grasp, Old Man Rom glanced at the profile of the girl perched on his shoulder—Petra.

"— — —"

Petra narrowed her large round eyes, her delicate features tensing as she maintained a serious watch over both battlefields without missing a beat.

The fight against "Gluttony" Roy Alphard and the swordsman who betrayed the kingdom—the "Backblade" Heinckel. Originally, the ringleader Aldebaran, his shinobi subordinate, and the "Divine Dragon" who had submitted to them were also present.

Though they had discussed breaking apart this dangerous group and dividing the battle, it wouldn't be an exaggeration to say Petra held the key to whether this strategy would succeed.

The plan had been formulated based on Clind's deep understanding of "Melancholy's" Authority, with everyone working together to make it succeed—but Petra had contributed the most.

Without her, this battle wouldn't have even begun. And that remained true even now.

"—hk!"

Petra bit her lip hard, her nails digging into Old Man Rom's shoulder as he crouched. Though her nails couldn't possibly hurt him, the unconscious gesture spoke volumes about the unimaginable strain she was under.

The burden of harboring a Witch Factor—the very thing that turned humans into "Witches" or Archbishops—was something only the bearer could truly understand. Moreover, Petra's role had originally been one Old Man Rom himself had been considered for.

They were the ones whose value lay not in direct combat but in quick thinking and judgment—exactly the positions Old Man Rom and Petra now occupied. In the end, their differing allegiances had decided who took which role, but Petra's burden could just as easily have been his.

That was why Old Man Rom had resolved that, while retrieving Felt was his top priority, his second was to do everything he could for Petra. To pour his entire soul into ensuring no oversights or failures in their battlefield decisions and commands, if only to lighten her burden even slightly.

"Flower three, Queen. Lightning two, Noble. Flower five, Hunter."

Scanning the battlefield, Old Man Rom relayed instructions just loud enough for Petra to hear. With each activation of her Authority, the nail marks on his shoulder deepened and multiplied.

Most of "Compression's" applications were reserved for the battle against "Gluttony." Roy seemed aware that Old Man Rom's group was influencing the battle's flow, but Ram's maneuvering was exceptional—she kept Roy's attention fixed on her, preventing him from interfering with their command.

Even with "Compression," the battle remained a razor-thin back-and-forth due to "Gluttony's" sheer versatility and options. In stark contrast, the other battlefield was defined by an overwhelming lack of options.

"—gh!"

Heinckel's pained grunts were drowned out by the sound of blows as he was pummeled relentlessly.

With Gaston joining Flam and Grassis, the twins' speed combined with his brute strength had turned the fight into what could only be called a one-sided beating—or perhaps an execution. Yet as long as Heinckel refused to go down, Flam and the others couldn't let up.

Both battlefields needed a decisive move to break the stalemate. And the moment Old Man Rom thought that—

"—Old Man Rom," Petra called out, meeting his gaze.

"— — —"

Their eyes locked, and in that instant, Old Man Rom understood they'd arrived at the same idea. Without even wasting time to nod, he focused on the perfect moment.

And then—

"Sun five, Queen—!"

At his command, Petra—her round eyes sharp with concentration—activated "Compression," perfectly timing it to amplify Ram and the others' coordinated strike against Roy.

"—Got him!"

Roy's small frame was sent flying by the wind, battered by the combined attack of the "Boar King" and two mabeasts. The spray of blood as he was launched into the air confirmed he'd taken serious damage.

At the last second, Roy had tried to use "Gluttony's" Authority on Ram, but it failed—creating the fatal opening that decided the battle. Old Man Rom couldn't help but marvel at Ram's nerve for setting that trap and Petra's ingenuity for suggesting it.

—Ram, now Ram Leite.

The unnatural adoption that exploited legal loopholes had been applied to all frontline members at risk of being targeted by "Gluttony"—a brilliant countermeasure against the Archbishop's schemes.

"But now..."

The situation had shifted. This was exactly the move they'd needed to break the deadlock. Clenching his large fist, Old Man Rom turned his attention to the other battlefield, hoping to capitalize on the momentum—

"...Nobody move. If you value this person's life, that is."

—only to be met with the worst possible development: Heinckel had Felt in a chokehold, a sword pressed to her throat.

