△▼△▼△▼△

—Of course, Felt's ability to cry out to her comrades in distress wasn't due to some convenient miracle of emotion, like something out of a fairy tale.

The cruelty of "Gluttony's" Authority had been demonstrated time and again by the tragedies of its victims and those around them. That such horrors could be undone by the power of feelings surrounding Felt was absurd.

The reason Filiolé had reverted to Felt was simple—she had never had her "memories" eaten by Roy in the first place.

"Here's the thing—seems we gotta eat Felt-chan's 'memories.' —Felt-chan, wanna work with us?"

Roy had proposed this right after Aldebaran decided to "handle" Felt, who had noticed too much and risked fracturing their group.

By having Roy consume the "memories" of what Felt had discovered, they could also dispose of her troublesome personality—always mouthing off and picking fights.

From Felt's perspective, losing her "memories" and ceasing to be herself was as good as death, but Aldebaran's methods were unacceptable either way.

"Yeah? Well, that don't mean I like you any better. What exactly you want me to do?"

"Haha~, love that attitude! But don't worry—detailed plans and perfect schemes aren't our style. What we want from you is simple: pretend your 'memories' got eaten."

"...Go on."

Felt squinted, seeing potential in Roy's offer. Delighted, Roy grinned from ear to ear.

"Sticking with the helmeted old men isn't bad, but if we don't act, we'll just get used and discarded—see these curse marks? We're in deep shit. So—"

"So?"

"Pretend your 'memories' are gone while secretly plotting payback. We'll use any opening you create to break free from our prisoner status."

"—Hah. What if I just tell the helmeted bastards and make you turn on each other?"

"Exactly! Do it! Go wild!"

Roy clapped excitedly, and though Felt tried to discern his true intentions, she quickly gave up. Even if he was hiding something, she couldn't see through it—he seemed completely genuine.

And honestly, his offer was a godsend for Felt. As things stood, she was powerless to stop her "memories" from being taken.

"Only catch is, to eat me, you need my name. Your bro was puking his guts out 'cause he didn't know it."

"Ah~, right. But somewhere deep down, don't you already know? That your real name's the same as that tragic princess?"

"— — —"

"Or do you wanna check? If 'Eclipse' works with that name, your 'memories' really will be gone—but at least you'll have proof. Well?"

"Tch, cheap provocation. —Fine, I'll play."

Roy licked his lips, leaning in. Felt snorted.

Who she really was—such a trivial question meant nothing to her. The idea that losing her "memories" was equivalent to death applied here too.

She had already lived her life as "Felt." Whatever her origins, that life had ended before it began.

She didn't need it. So she'd play along with "Gluttony's" scheme.

"I'm the only one winning this."

"Kuku~, ahaha! Knew you'd say that! Believed in you! But we're taking our own insurance—can't let you win too easily."

"Insurance? How lame. Go all in."

"Brave words, but pride means nothing to us. —Eat or be eaten. That's all."

With that, Roy clicked his teeth, celebrating their secret pact.

True to his word, Roy pretended to consume Felt's "memories," leaving her intact. Felt, half-doubting their agreement, played her part—pretending to have lost her memories, acting as Filiolé Lugunica, a royal she knew nothing about.

"Sorry, but the only reference I had was Crusch-nee."

Having seen Crusch's drastic personality shift after her "memories" were eaten, Felt modeled Filiolé after her. Surprisingly, Aldebaran's group—especially Heinckel—seemed to buy it.

Fortunately, her act as Filiolé was brief—Aldebaran soon sealed her inside a strange black sphere. The sensation inside was suffocating and unpleasant, but it had one advantage.

Less time acting as Filiolé meant fewer chances to slip up. If Felt made a mistake, Roy's "insurance" would activate—as he'd threatened.

The "insurance" he'd prepared to ensure she had no choice but to cooperate—and to prevent betrayal afterward.

It was—

"—It's coming out of my shadow!!"

Even as Heinckel held her in a chokehold with a sword to her neck, Felt screamed.

The final trump card "Gluttony" Roy Alphard had prepared to deceive Aldebaran's group and escape—the third of the three great mabeasts alongside the "White Whale" and "Great Rabbit"— 

"—The Black Serpent!!"

—the "Black Serpent," the plague-bearing mabeast that had claimed more lives than any other since its birth, now answered the breached pact's call, descending upon the battlefield where both factions clashed at full strength.
